  "id": "COMPOUND:425 - DISEASE:886",
  "verbalization": "Allopurinol, through its interaction with DnaJ heat shock protein family (Hsp40) member B6, appears to influence the development of Seborrhea NOS, which in turn is linked to immunoglobulin kappa variable 2D-29 and ultimately to Double Outlet Right Ventricle. This pathway suggests a potential role for allopurinol in the pathogenesis of this cardiac condition, though the exact mechanism remains unclear. The evidence is consistent across multiple pathways, indicating a possible involvement of Hsp40 and its downstream effects on immune-related proteins. The observed relationship highlights a complex interplay between allopurinol, immune modulation, and cardiac development, underscoring the need for further investigation into the specific molecular mechanisms at play.",
